<title>USA: TIG says board oks increasing buyback.</title>
<headline>TIG says board oks increasing buyback.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>TIG Holdings Inc said Thursday its board of directors has approved an increase of 2.5 million shares in its repurchase program to a total of 16.25 million shares.</p>
<p>The company said the initial authorization was announced in March 1994 and has been followed by ten subsequent increases, including this one.</p>
<p>The company said it has repurchased 12,398,836 common shares to date, or 19.4 percent of the common shares outstanding at the program's inception, at an aggregate cost of $345.8 million, or $27.89 per share.</p>
<p>The company has 52,799,625 common shares outstanding.</p>
